## Proof Detail, Not Material Difference

Five supplemental-proof notes are accepted, with exact task/field pointers
in review.json:

- 1038: FIRST /tasks/6/branches/4 supplies an explicit no-partition proof
  for the both-pieces-similar-to-original referent. Author
  /tasks/6/interpretation_caveat does not assert that referent or a competing
  solution. Do not mistake the shorter treatment for a different valid answer.
- 1042a: Author /tasks/13/degenerate_and_zero_coefficient_cases adds
  general-b middle-coefficient/discriminant discussion. It does not change
  the unique specified-root parameter or create degree degeneration.
- 1042b: Author /tasks/14/degenerate_and_zero_coefficient_cases adds
  general-b zero-middle-coefficient and root-count intervals. The selected
  b=-17 and all roots match.
- 1042c: Author /tasks/15/degenerate_and_zero_coefficient_cases includes
  the matching b=1 linear branch, plus additional b=-1 and discriminant cases.
  Its factorization after multiplying the equation by 2 is equivalent, not
  a coefficient mismatch.
- 1042d: Author /tasks/16/degenerate_and_zero_coefficient_cases includes
  the matching b=5 linear branch, plus general b=-2, b=0 and discriminant cases.
  These additional cases do not satisfy the uniquely selected parameter.

The author's supplemental general-parameter classifications were inspected,
not independently recomputed. This static comparison does not claim a new
arithmetic certification for claims outside the frozen specified-root solve.

1039's author primary/conditional labels preserve, rather than erase, the same
two readings as FIRST. In 1040, author side variables u,v map to FIRST x,y;
they are not FIRST's intercept variables u,v. Root order and exact-number
representations also do not constitute findings.

Source qualifications for 1035b, 1038, 1039 and 1040 remain recorded but are
not comparison failures. Figure-66 relationship and visual approval for
1037b remain outside scope; no visual approval is granted.

